  "solution": {
    "text": "Methane leads to both global warming&nbsp;&amp; photochemical smog. Methane is generated in large amounts from paddy fields. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> can be absorbed by photosynthesis, or by formation of acid rain etc., while no such activities are there for methane. Hence methane is stronger global warming gas than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, Methane is not a component of reducing smog.",
